{
  "type": "Collection",
  "id": "alternaria-tomato-risk-po-valley",
  "stac_version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "For every processing-tomato field classified from Sentinel-2 in Piedmont, Lombardy, Veneto and Emilia-Romagna (Italy), seasons 2020 to 2025, the ALT-tomato model (Salotti et al., 2026) was run from the field's own Sentinel-2 transplant date to its own harvest date, with the hourly ERA5-Land weather of the 0.1° cell the field lies in. The model was run at four disease management levels, and a 3,000-draw Monte Carlo propagated the management, transplant-date and inoculum uncertainty. Every value is a direct model run: no emulator, no interpolation.",
